body:
**[comments] Rule 2, restates identifiers: shorten**

Sentences two and three restate the #ifdef TRON_K_VNNI and the head_size == HEAD_SIZE_128 test below. The facts the code does not say are that TRON_K_VNNI comes from CMake and that the gate ignores the query type and AMX availability, which is the invariant the Note [K VNNI storage] also states.

Proposed:
```cpp
// The layout gate. TRON_K_VNNI is a CMake option. The gate depends on the head
// size only, not on the query type or on AMX availability. So every reader and
// writer of a slot sees the same layout.
```

Line-to-code mapping (Rule 4):
line 1 (CMake option) -> #ifdef TRON_K_VNNI; line 2 (head size only) -> layout_on = head_size == HEAD_SIZE_128, the only parameter; line 3 (same layout for every reader and writer) -> the two definitions take no other input
